// @run
// @log 1
// @log 0
// A `(Circle | null)[]` WHERE `Circle` IS A UNION ARM — the niche list D771 closed, and the
// declaration that used to break it is the only reason it ever broke.
//
// WHAT THE REFUSAL WAS. `emitProgram: a nullable-Circle list element has no rep; use a
// non-null element type`. Delete `type Shape = Circle | Sq` from this file and the identical
// list RUNS on master: the sentence was never about `(Circle | null)[]`, it was about a
// `(Circle | null)[]` in a module where some declared union names `Circle`. `collectS`
// withholds an `sNames` row from a union member, so `refArrShapeKind`'s `(P | null)[]` niche
// arm (`structIndexByName`) answered -1, the ladder fell through to its kind-2 union-box
// return, and `collectA` refused a niche nullable there — correctly, since a box has no rep
// for a niche. Every rung behaved as written and the classification was lost two rungs up.
//
// WHY IT NEEDED NO NEW REP. Since D280 an arm and its declared layout twin share ONE WasmGC
// heap (`uVarHeap[vi] = sHeapIdx[uVarSTwinAt(vi)]`), and the interned element NAME keeps the
// `| null` spelling, whose heap `rlElemVariantHeap` already resolves through `nonNulBaseOf` +
// `variantIndexOf`. Disassembled, the list backing is `(array (mut (ref null $Circle)))` and
// the literal is a bare `struct.new $Circle` — the union box is minted (because `Shape` is
// declared) and untouched.
//
// THE SECOND LEG IS D772's, AND IT IS HERE BECAUSE D771 ALONE MAKES IT WORSE. `const hole =
// []` bound to the same annotation is the EMPTY literal, whose element the annotation
// synthesis has to render; `nodeArrayElemName` covered exactly one nullable element (a
// closure), so every other one built the i32-list default into a ref-list cell — check-clean
// invalid wasm, at `(i32 | null)[]` and `(Dot | null)[]` as much as here, on master and with
// no union in sight. With D771 alone this leg goes from a loud reject to a SILENT class,
// which is why the two rungs ship together and why both legs are pinned in one file.
//
// WHAT IS STILL REFUSED, DELIBERATELY UNPINNED HERE AND RECORDED IN D771: a NARROWED FIELD
// READ off the niche element (`const e = a[0]  if e != null { print(e.r) }`) is
// `emitProgram: field access but no struct type declared` — the same missing `sNames` row,
// one resolver further on. It is a loud reject and it is reachable only because the list
// now builds; the same read with no union declared runs, and with a non-null `Circle[]`
// element it runs too.
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq

function f() {
  const xs = [{ r: 7 }]
  const a: (Circle | null)[] = xs
  print(a.length)
  const hole = []
  const b: (Circle | null)[] = hole
  print(b.length)
}

f()
